body:
### Describe the bug

When `resolveChildWorkflowExecutionStart` receives a failed or cancelled result, the `childWorkflowComplete` completion map still holds an entry for that sequence number. Since the child workflow never started, it will never complete, so this entry is orphaned and constitutes a memory leak for the duration of the workflow execution.

#### Suggested fix

In `packages/workflow/src/internals.ts`, in the `resolveChildWorkflowExecutionStart` method, delete the corresponding `childWorkflowComplete` entry when the start fails or is cancelled:
```
} else if (activation.failed) {
  // Child workflow failed to start — clean up the orphaned completion entry
  reject(new ChildWorkflowFailure(...));
  this.completions.childWorkflowComplete.delete(seq);
} else if (activation.cancelled) {
  // Child workflow start was cancelled — clean up the orphaned completion entry
  reject(this.failureToError(activation.cancelled.failure));
  this.completions.childWorkflowComplete.delete(seq);
}
```

#### Impact

Low risk. The orphaned entry is small (one Map entry per failed child start) and only matters for long-running workflows that repeatedly fail to start children.
